  "summary": "The aesthetic of granite surfaces finished with a honed rather than polished surface for a matte appearance.",
  "description": "Characterized by the natural crystalline structure of granite with a smooth, non-reflective finish that enhances the stone's natural texture while hiding fingerprints and imperfections. Developed as an alternative to traditional polished granite, offering a more subtle, contemporary look for residential and commercial applications.",
  "culturalContext": "Honed granite — the matte-finish counterpoint to glossy polished stone — became the 2010s-20s \"quiet luxury\" surface: flamed, leathered and honed finishes scattering light softly, hiding etch and fingerprint, reading as chalk-like sophistication in kitchens and lobby floors. The finish's slip-resistance made it commercial-standard; design discourse framed honed stone against \"builder gloss\" as taste marker, and leathered-granite texture is now a countertop-culture staple.",
